Here is the documented file:

```
-- | Adequacy of the weakest precondition for the heap language.
-- |
-- | This module establishes the *adequacy theorem* of Iris: the soundness bridge
-- | that connects the internal logic (separation-logic judgements about `wp`) to
-- | external, meta-level facts about the operational semantics. Concretely it proves:
-- |
-- |   * `wp_adequacy`  — if `True ⊢ wp e {v. φ v}` holds and `e` reduces in `k`
-- |                      physical steps to a value `v` (in some final state), then
-- |                      the pure proposition `φ v` holds at the meta level.
-- |   * `wp_progress`  — under the same hypothesis, every configuration `(e', σ')`
-- |                      reachable from `(e, σ)` is `not_stuck`: `e'` is either a
-- |                      value or able to take a primitive step (safety).
-- |
-- | The proof follows the standard Iris recipe. The state interpretation here is the
-- | heap authority `own_heap_auth σ` (a `●`-element of the heap `CMRA`, the analogue
-- | of Iris's `state_interp`). The skeleton is:
-- |
-- |   1. `ghost_intro`  — frame the state interpretation alongside the `wp` (seeding
-- |                       the run from the initial heap).
-- |   2. `wp_step`      — one physical step turns `wp e ∗ S(σ)` into `|==> ▷ |==> (S(σ₂) ∗ wp e₂)`,
-- |                       mirroring the `wp_pre` unfolding (reducibility + step preservation).
-- |   3. `wp_steps`     — iterate `wp_step` over a `k`-step reduction, producing a
-- |                       `(|==> ▷)ᵏ` tower (`bupd_later_iter`).
-- |   4. soundness      — `bupd_later_iter_soundness` (from `updates`) extracts a pure
-- |                       proposition out of the `(|==> ▷)ᵏ` tower at step-index `k`,
-- |                       using that the initial heap authority is valid at every index.
-- |
-- | Everything is phrased over the step-indexed model `uPred (HeapCMRA …)` of `OFE`s and
-- | `CMRA`s: `mkProperSep`/`mkProperBUpd`/`mkProperLater`/… are the separating conjunction,
-- | basic update (`|==>`) and later (`▷`) modalities, and `properUPred_ent` is `⊢`.
\import Order.PartialOrder
\import Data.Maybe
\import Arith.Nat
\import Data.Or
\import Logic
\import Paths
\import interface
\import uPred
\import cmra
\import lang
\import weakestpre
\import ofe
\import updates
\import lib.heap
\import lib.gmap_cmra
\import lib.excl_cmra
\import lib.pmap


-- =================================================================================
-- Lemma 1: Ghost State Introduction
-- =================================================================================


-- | Seed the verification with the state interpretation: from the heap authority
-- | `own_heap_auth σ` alone we may produce `own_heap_auth σ ∗ wp e {Φ}`, given that
-- | `wp e {Φ}` holds out of the trivial resource (`True ⊢ wp e {Φ}`).
-- |
-- | This is the entry point of the adequacy run — it pairs the freshly-owned full view
-- | of the heap with the weakest precondition. The witnessing decomposition uses the
-- | whole element `a` for the authority and the unit for the `wp`, which is valid by
-- | `ucmra_unit_valid`; `hwp` then supplies the `wp` from the trivial premise.
\lemma ghost_intro
  {cnt : Countable Loc}
  (e     : Expr)
  (Phi   : Value -> ProperUPred (HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value))
  (sigma : State cnt)
  (hwp   : properUPred_ent (mkProperPure (\Sigma)) (wp e Phi))
  : properUPred_ent
    (own_heap_auth sigma)
    (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi))
  =>
    \let M => HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value
    \in \lam n a hv hauth =>
        inP (a, M.unit,
             transport (\lam w => M.dist n a w)
                 (inv (ucmra_unit_right_id a))
                 (M.ofe_dist_refl n a),
             hauth,
             hwp n M.unit ((M.cmra_valid_validN M.unit).1 M.ucmra_unit_valid n) ())


-- =================================================================================
-- Lemma 2: WP Step
-- =================================================================================

-- | Single physical step of the adequacy run: given a primitive step
-- | `e σ → e₂ σ₂`, the resources `wp e {Φ} ∗ S(σ)` entail `|==> ▷ |==> (S(σ₂) ∗ wp e₂ {Φ})`
-- | (where `S = own_heap_auth`). This is the operational core, derived directly from the
-- | `wp_pre` fixpoint unfolding.
-- |
-- | Proof idea: unfold `wp e {Φ}` via `wp_unfold`. Since `e` steps it is not a value
-- | (`val_stuck`), so the unfolded `wp` is the `∀σ'. S(σ') -∗ |==> (Reducible e σ' ∧ ▷ ∀…)`
-- | clause. Instantiate it at `σ`, feed in the state interpretation (the wand), and obtain
-- | the reducibility-and-later-step-preservation under `|==>`. Then `bupd_mono` rewrites
-- | the `∧`-body: at step-index `suc k` the `▷`-guarded universally-quantified step
-- | preservation is instantiated at the concrete `e₂`/`σ₂` and the actual `hstep`,
-- | yielding `|==> (S(σ₂) ∗ wp e₂ {Φ})` one step later.
\lemma wp_step
  {cnt : Countable Loc}
  (e e2        : Expr)
  (Phi         : Value -> ProperUPred (HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value))
  (sigma sigma2 : State cnt)
  (hstep       : PrimStep e sigma e2 sigma2)
  : properUPred_ent
    (mkProperSep (wp e Phi) (own_heap_auth sigma))
    (mkProperBUpd (mkProperLater (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma2) (wp e2 Phi)))))
  =>
    \lam n a hv hsep =>
        \case hsep \with {
          | inP (a_wp, a_auth, dist_a, hwp, hauth) =>
            \let M => HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value
                 | tv_nothing : to_val e = nothing =>
                   val_stuck e sigma e2 sigma2 hstep
                 | hv_op : M.validN n (M.op a_wp a_auth) =>
                   M.cmra_validN_ne n a (M.op a_wp a_auth) dist_a hv
                 | hv_wp : M.validN n a_wp => M.cmra_validN_op_l n a_wp a_auth hv_op
                 | hwp_unfolded : (wp_pre wp e Phi).upred_holds n a_wp =>
                   (wp_unfold e Phi n a_wp hv_wp).1 hwp
                 | hwand : (mkProperWand (own_heap_auth sigma)
                     (mkProperBUpd (mkProperAnd
                         (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma))
                         (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                             mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                                 mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma e' s'))
                                     (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi)))))))))
                           ).upred_holds n a_wp =>
                   \let
                     | unfolded_eq : wp_pre wp  e Phi =
                     mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam sigma' =>
                         mkProperWand (own_heap_auth sigma')
                             (mkProperBUpd (mkProperAnd
                                 (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma'))
                                 (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                                     mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                                         mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma' e' s'))
                                             (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi)))))))))) =>
                       pmap (\lam tv =>
                           \case tv \with {
                             | just v  => mkProperBUpd (Phi v)
                             | nothing => mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam sigma' =>
                                 mkProperWand (own_heap_auth sigma')
                                     (mkProperBUpd (mkProperAnd
                                         (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma'))
                                         (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                                             mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                                                 mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma' e' s'))
                                                     (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi))))))))))
                           })
                           tv_nothing
                     | hforall :
                           (mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam sigma' =>
                               mkProperWand (own_heap_auth sigma')
                                   (mkProperBUpd (mkProperAnd
                                       (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma'))
                                       (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                                           mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                                               mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma' e' s'))
                                                   (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi)))))))))
                           )).upred_holds n a_wp =>
                       transport
                           (\lam (P : ProperUPred (HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value)) => P.upred_holds n a_wp)
                           unfolded_eq
                           hwp_unfolded
                   \in hforall sigma
                 | h_on_op : (mkProperBUpd (mkProperAnd
                     (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma))
                     (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                         mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                             mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma e' s'))
                                 (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi)))))))
                                      )).upred_holds n (M.op a_wp a_auth) =>
                   hwand n <=-refl a_auth hv_op hauth
                 | h_on_a : (mkProperBUpd (mkProperAnd
                     (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma))
                     (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                         mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                             mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma e' s'))
                                 (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi)))))))
                                     )).upred_holds n a =>
                   \let
                     | dist_a_op_unit : M.dist n a (M.op (M.op a_wp a_auth) M.unit) =>
                       transport (\lam w => M.dist n a w)
                           (inv (ucmra_unit_right_id (M.op a_wp a_auth)))
                           dist_a
                   \in
                         (mkProperBUpd (mkProperAnd
                             (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma))
                             (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                                 mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                                     mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma e' s'))
                                         (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi)))))))
                                  )).upred_mono n n (M.op a_wp a_auth) a
                         h_on_op
                         (inP (M.unit, dist_a_op_unit))
                         <=-refl
            \in
              bupd_mono
                  (mkProperAnd
                      (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma))
                      (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                          mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                              mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma e' s'))
                                  (mkProperBUpd(mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi))))))))
                  (mkProperLater (mkProperBUpd(mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma2) (wp e2 Phi))))
                  (\lam n' a' hv' hand =>
                      \case n' \as n'', hv' \as hv'' : (HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value).validN n'' a',
                            hand \as hand'' : (mkProperAnd
                                (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma))
                                (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                                    mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                                        mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma e' s'))
                                            (mkProperBUpd(mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi)))))
                                ))).upred_holds n'' a' \return
                          (mkProperLater (mkProperBUpd(mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma2) (wp e2 Phi)))).upred_holds n'' a'
                      \with {
                        | 0, _, _ => ()
                        | suc k, hv'', hand'' =>
                          \let hlater : (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                              mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                                  mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma e' s'))
                                      (mkProperBUpd(mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi)))))).upred_holds k a' =>
                            hand''.2
                          \in hlater e2 sigma2 k <=-refl a'
                              (inP (M.unit,
                                    transport (\lam w => M.dist k a' w)
                                        (inv (ucmra_unit_right_id a'))
                                        (M.ofe_dist_refl k a')))
                              ((HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value).cmra_validN_le (suc k) k a' hv'' (n<=sucn k))
                              hstep
                      })
                  n a hv h_on_a
        }


-- =================================================================================
-- Multi-step reduction
-- =================================================================================

-- | `Steps k e σ e' σ'` is the `k`-fold iteration of the primitive step relation:
-- | a chain of exactly `k` `PrimStep`s from configuration `(e, σ)` to `(e', σ')`.
-- | `StepsRefl` is the empty (0-step) chain; `StepsStep` prepends one head step.
-- | Truncated to `\Prop` because adequacy only needs the existence of such a chain.
\truncated \data Steps {cnt : Countable Loc} (k : Nat) (e : Expr) (sigma : State cnt) (e' : Expr) (sigma' : State cnt) : \Prop \elim k
  | 0      => StepsRefl (pe : e = e') (ps : sigma = sigma')
  | suc k' => StepsStep
    (emid : Expr) (smid : State cnt)
    (hd   : PrimStep e sigma emid smid)
    (tl   : Steps k' emid smid e' sigma')

-- | `k`-fold iteration of the `|==> ▷ -` modality applied to `P`, i.e. `(|==> ▷)ᵏ P`.
-- | This is the modal "tower" that a `k`-step weakest-precondition run accumulates;
-- | thin wrapper around `bupd_later_iter_fn` from `updates`.
\func bupd_later_iter
  {cnt : Countable Loc}
  (k  : Nat)
  (P  : ProperUPred (HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value))
  : ProperUPred (HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value)
  => bupd_later_iter_fn k P

-- | Safety predicate at the meta level: configuration `(e, σ)` is *not stuck* if `e`
-- | is already a value or `e` is reducible in `σ` (can take a primitive step).
-- | This is the postcondition of the progress half of adequacy.
\func not_stuck {cnt : Countable Loc} (e : Expr) (sigma : State cnt) : \Prop =>
  (\Sigma (v : Value) (to_val e = just v)) ||
  (Reducible e sigma)


-- | A `wp` together with the state interpretation entails that the current
-- | configuration is not stuck: `S(σ) ∗ wp e {Φ} ⊢ |==> ⌜not_stuck e σ⌝`.
-- |
-- | Proof idea: case on `to_val e`. If `e` is a value the conclusion is the left
-- | disjunct immediately (`bupd_intro`). Otherwise unfold `wp` to its non-value clause,
-- | feed the state interpretation through the wand at `σ`, obtaining `|==> (Reducible e σ ∧ …)`,
-- | and `bupd_mono` projects out the reducibility conjunct as the right disjunct of `not_stuck`.
-- | (Several `cmra_comm`/`transport` steps reconcile the order of the separating product
-- | with the resource `a` carried by the entailment.)
\lemma wp_not_stuck
  {cnt : Countable Loc}
  (e     : Expr)
  (Phi   : Value -> ProperUPred (HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value))
  (sigma : State cnt)
  : properUPred_ent
    (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi))
    (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (not_stuck e sigma)))
  =>
    \lam n a hv hsep =>
        \case hsep \with {
          | inP (a_auth, a_wp, dist_a, hauth, hwp) =>
            \let
              | M => HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value
              | hv_op : M.validN n (M.op a_auth a_wp) =>
                M.cmra_validN_ne n a (M.op a_auth a_wp) dist_a hv
              | hv_wp : M.validN n a_wp =>
                M.cmra_validN_op_l n a_wp a_auth
                    (transport (\lam w => M.validN n w) (M.cmra_comm a_auth a_wp) hv_op)
              | hwp_unfolded : (wp_pre wp e Phi).upred_holds n a_wp =>
                (wp_unfold e Phi n a_wp hv_wp).1 hwp
            \in \case to_val e \as tv, idp : to_val e = tv \return
                (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (not_stuck e sigma))).upred_holds n a
            \with {
              | just v, p_val =>
                \let
                  | h_val : not_stuck e sigma => byLeft (v, p_val)
                  | h_pure : (mkProperPure (not_stuck e sigma)).upred_holds n a => h_val
                \in bupd_intro (mkProperPure (not_stuck e sigma)) n a hv h_pure
              | nothing, p_noval =>
                \let
                  | unfolded_eq : wp_pre wp e Phi =
                  mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam sigma' =>
                      mkProperWand (own_heap_auth sigma')
                          (mkProperBUpd (mkProperAnd
                              (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma'))
                              (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                                  mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                                      mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma' e' s'))
                                          (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi)))))))))) =>
                    pmap (\lam tv =>
                        \case tv \with {
                          | just v  => mkProperBUpd (Phi v)
                          | nothing => mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam sigma' =>
                              mkProperWand (own_heap_auth sigma')
                                  (mkProperBUpd (mkProperAnd
                                      (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma'))
                                      (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                                          mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                                              mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma' e' s'))
                                                  (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi))))))))))
                        })
                        p_noval
                  | hforall :
                        (mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam sigma' =>
                            mkProperWand (own_heap_auth sigma')
                                (mkProperBUpd (mkProperAnd
                                    (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma'))
                                    (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                                        mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                                            mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma' e' s'))
                                                (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi)))))))))
                        )).upred_holds n a_wp =>
                    transport
                        (\lam (P : ProperUPred (HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value)) => P.upred_holds n a_wp)
                        unfolded_eq
                        hwp_unfolded
                  | hwand : (mkProperWand (own_heap_auth sigma)
                      (mkProperBUpd (mkProperAnd
                          (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma))
                          (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                              mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                                  mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma e' s'))
                                      (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi)))))))))
                            ).upred_holds n a_wp =>
                    hforall sigma
                  | hv_wp_auth : M.validN n (M.op a_wp a_auth) =>
                    transport (\lam w => M.validN n w) (M.cmra_comm a_auth a_wp) hv_op
                  | h_on_wp_auth : (mkProperBUpd (mkProperAnd
                      (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma))
                      (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                          mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                              mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma e' s'))
                                  (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi)))))))
                                            )).upred_holds n (M.op a_wp a_auth) =>
                    hwand n <=-refl a_auth hv_wp_auth hauth
                  | dist_a_wp_auth : M.dist n a (M.op a_wp a_auth) =>
                    M.ofe_dist_trans n a (M.op a_auth a_wp) (M.op a_wp a_auth)
                        dist_a
                        (transport (\lam w => M.dist n (M.op a_auth a_wp) w)
                            (M.cmra_comm a_auth a_wp)
                            (M.ofe_dist_refl n (M.op a_auth a_wp)))
                  | h_on_a : (mkProperBUpd (mkProperAnd
                      (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma))
                      (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                          mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                              mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma e' s'))
                                  (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi)))))))
                                      )).upred_holds n a =>
                    \let
                      | dist_a_op_unit : M.dist n a (M.op (M.op a_wp a_auth) M.unit) =>
                        transport (\lam w => M.dist n a w)
                            (inv (ucmra_unit_right_id (M.op a_wp a_auth)))
                            dist_a_wp_auth
                    \in
                          (mkProperBUpd (mkProperAnd
                              (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma))
                              (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                                  mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                                      mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma e' s'))
                                          (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi)))))))
                                   )).upred_mono n n (M.op a_wp a_auth) a
                          h_on_wp_auth
                          (inP (M.unit, dist_a_op_unit))
                          <=-refl
                \in
                  bupd_mono
                      (mkProperAnd
                          (mkProperPure (Reducible e sigma))
                          (mkProperLater (mkProperForall Expr (\lam e' =>
                              mkProperForall (State cnt) (\lam s' =>
                                  mkProperImpl (mkProperPure (PrimStep e sigma e' s'))
                                      (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth s') (wp e' Phi))))))))
                      (mkProperPure (not_stuck e sigma))
                      (\lam n' a' hv' hand => byRight hand.1)
                      n a hv h_on_a
            }
        }

-- =================================================================================
-- Lemma 3: WP Steps — k-step iteration
-- =================================================================================


-- | Iterated step lemma: a `k`-step reduction `e σ →ᵏ e' σ'` lifts `wp_step` to
-- | `|==> (S(σ) ∗ wp e {Φ}) ⊢ (|==> ▷)ᵏ |==> (S(σ') ∗ wp e' {Φ})`, where `S = own_heap_auth`.
-- | This collapses an entire run of the machine into the modal tower `bupd_later_iter`.
-- |
-- | Proof by induction on the step chain. The base case (`StepsRefl`) is reflexivity
-- | after transporting along the equalities `e = e'`, `σ = σ'`. The inductive case takes
-- | the head step with `wp_step` to reach `smid`/`emid` under `|==> ▷ |==>`, applies the
-- | induction hypothesis to the tail under the `▷` (peeling one step index with
-- | `cmra_validN_le`), and stitches the modalities together with `bupd_trans`/`bupd_mono`.
\lemma wp_steps
  {cnt : Countable Loc}
  (k     : Nat)
  (e e'  : Expr)
  (Phi   : Value -> ProperUPred (HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value))
  (sigma sigma' : State cnt)
  (hsteps : Steps k e sigma e' sigma')
  : properUPred_ent
    (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi)))
    (bupd_later_iter k (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp e' Phi))))
\elim k, hsteps
  | 0, StepsRefl pe ps =>
    transport
        (\lam x => properUPred_ent
            (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi)))
            (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth x.2) (wp x.1 Phi))))
        (path (\lam i => (pe @ i, ps @ i)))
        (properUPred_ent_refl (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi))))
  | suc k', StepsStep emid smid hd tl =>
    \let ih : properUPred_ent
        (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth smid) (wp emid Phi)))
        (bupd_later_iter k' (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp e' Phi)))) =>
      wp_steps k' emid e' Phi smid sigma' tl
    \in \lam n a hv h_bupd_own_wp =>
        bupd_trans
            (mkProperLater (bupd_later_iter k'
                (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp e' Phi)))))
            n a hv
            (bupd_mono
                (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi))
                (mkProperBUpd (mkProperLater (bupd_later_iter k'
                    (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp e' Phi))))))
                (\lam n' a' hv' hsep_own_wp =>
                    \let hsep_wp_own : (mkProperSep (wp e Phi) (own_heap_auth sigma)).upred_holds n' a' =>
                           \case hsep_own_wp \with {
                             | inP (ao, aw, d, ho, hw) =>
                               inP (aw, ao,
                                    transport (\lam w => (HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value).dist n' a' w)
                                        ((HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value).cmra_comm ao aw)
                                        d,
                                    hw, ho)
                           }
                         | h_one : (mkProperBUpd (mkProperLater
                             (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth smid) (wp emid Phi))))).upred_holds n' a' =>
                           wp_step e emid Phi sigma smid hd n' a' hv' hsep_wp_own
                         | h_iter : (mkProperBUpd (mkProperLater
                             (bupd_later_iter k'
                                 (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp e' Phi)))))).upred_holds n' a' =>
                           bupd_mono
                               (mkProperLater (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth smid) (wp emid Phi))))
                               (mkProperLater (bupd_later_iter k'
                                   (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp e' Phi)))))
                               (\lam n'' a'' hv'' hlater =>
                                   \case n'' \as nnn,
                                         hv'' \as hv_nnn : (HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value).validN nnn a'',
                                         hlater \as hlater' :
                                             (mkProperLater (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth smid) (wp emid Phi)))).upred_holds nnn a''
                                   \return
                                       (mkProperLater (bupd_later_iter k'
                                           (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp e' Phi))))).upred_holds nnn a''
                                   \with {
                                     | 0, _, _ => ()
                                     | suc m, hv_nnn, h_bupd_smid =>
                                       ih m a'' ((HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value).cmra_validN_le (suc m) m a'' hv_nnn (n<=sucn m)) h_bupd_smid
                                   })
                               n' a' hv' h_one
                    \in h_iter)
                n a hv h_bupd_own_wp)

-- =================================================================================
-- Lemma 4: bupd_later_soundness
-- =================================================================================


-- | Soundness of the `|==> ▷` tower for extracting a pure proposition: if the heap
-- | authority for `σ` entails `(|==> ▷)ⁿ |==> ⌜P⌝` *for every* step index `n`, then `P`
-- | holds at the meta level. (Specialised to depth `n = 0` here, the base of the tower.)
-- |
-- | Proof: build the initial authority element `a₀ = heap_auth (state→gmap σ)`, show it is
-- | valid at index 0 (validity of the heap gmap plus trivial inclusion of the empty map),
-- | feed it to `h 0` to get `(|==> ⌜P⌝)` at index 0, and conclude with `bupd_extract_pure`.
\lemma bupd_later_soundness
  {cnt : Countable Loc}
  (P     : \Prop)
  (sigma : State cnt)
  (h     : \Pi (n : Nat) ->
      properUPred_ent
          (own_heap_auth sigma)
          (bupd_later_iter n (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure P))))
  : P =>
  \let
    | M => HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value
    | a0 => heap_auth (heap_state_to_gmap sigma)
    | hv_a0 : M.validN 0 a0 =>
      \let
        | G   => GmapUCMRA Loc cnt (ExclUCMRA (DiscreteOFE Value))
        | g   => heap_state_to_gmap sigma
        | hv_g : G.validN 0 g => heap_state_to_gmap_validN 0 sigma
        | hincl : inclN {G} {\new Op G.E { | op => G.op }} gempty 0 g =>
          inP (g,
               transport (\lam w => G.dist 0 g w)
                   (inv (G.ucmra_unit_left_id g))
                   (G.ofe_dist_refl 0 g))
      \in (hv_g, hincl)
    | hauth_a0 : (own_heap_auth sigma).upred_holds 0 a0 =>
      inP (M.unit,
           transport (\lam w => M.dist 0 a0 w)
               (inv (ucmra_unit_right_id a0))
               (M.ofe_dist_refl 0 a0))
    | h_bupd_pure : (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure P)).upred_holds 0 a0 =>
      h 0 0 a0 hv_a0 hauth_a0
  \in bupd_extract_pure P 0 a0 hv_a0 h_bupd_pure


-- =================================================================================
-- Lemma 5: WP Adequacy
-- =================================================================================


-- | Extract a pure proposition out of the `(|==> ▷)ᵏ |==> ⌜φ⌝` tower at step index `k`,
-- | given a resource `a` valid at `k`. Thin wrapper around `bupd_later_iter_soundness`;
-- | the final step of both adequacy theorems below.
\lemma bupd_later_iter_extract_pure
  {cnt : Countable Loc}
  (k   : Nat)
  (phi : \Prop)
  (a   : (HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value).E)
  (hv  : (HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value).validN k a)
  (h   : (bupd_later_iter k (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure phi))).upred_holds k a)
  : phi =>
  bupd_later_iter_soundness k phi a hv h


-- | Adequacy of `wp` (correctness half): if `True ⊢ wp e {v. ⌜φ v⌝}` and `e σ` reduces
-- | in `k` steps to a value `v` in state `σ'`, then the meta-level proposition `φ v` holds.
-- | This is the central soundness theorem: a separation-logic Hoare-style judgement about
-- | `e` yields a genuine fact about the value the program computes.
-- |
-- | Proof pipeline (composing the lemmas above):
-- |   * `h_seed`  : `S(σ) ⊢ |==> (S(σ) ∗ wp e {Φ})`           — `ghost_intro` then `bupd_intro`.
-- |   * `h_run`   : push through the `k`-step reduction with `wp_steps`, reaching
-- |                 `(|==> ▷)ᵏ |==> (S(σ') ∗ wp (Val v) {Φ})`.
-- |   * collapse the value: `wp (Val v) {Φ} ≡ |==> Φ v` (`wp_value`), then drop the now-pure
-- |     `Φ v = ⌜φ v⌝` out of the separation with the authority (`inner_drop`) and flatten the
-- |     nested `|==>` via `bupd_trans`; `iter_mono_aux` lifts this through the modal tower.
-- |   * `h_final` : `S(σ) ⊢ (|==> ▷)ᵏ |==> ⌜φ v⌝`, evaluated at index `k` on the valid initial
-- |     authority `a₀`, and discharged by `bupd_later_iter_soundness`.
\lemma wp_adequacy
  {cnt : Countable Loc}
  (e      : Expr)
  (phi    : Value -> \Prop)
  (sigma  : State cnt)
  (k      : Nat)
  (v      : Value)
  (sigma' : State cnt)
  (hwp    : properUPred_ent
      (mkProperPure (\Sigma))
      (wp e (\lam w => mkProperPure (phi w))))
  (hsteps : Steps k e sigma (Val v) sigma')
  : phi v =>
  \let
    | M => HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value
    | Phi : Value -> ProperUPred (HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value) =>
      \lam w => mkProperPure (phi w)
    | a0 => heap_auth (heap_state_to_gmap sigma)
    | hv_a0 : \Pi (n : Nat) -> M.validN n a0 =>
      \lam n =>
          \let
            | G => GmapUCMRA Loc cnt (ExclUCMRA (DiscreteOFE Value))
            | g => heap_state_to_gmap sigma
            | hv_g : G.validN n g => heap_state_to_gmap_validN n sigma
            | hincl : inclN {G} {\new Op G.E { | op => G.op }} gempty n g =>
              inP (g, transport (\lam w => G.dist n g w)
                  (inv (G.ucmra_unit_left_id g))
                  (G.ofe_dist_refl n g))
          \in (hv_g, hincl)
    | hauth_a0 : \Pi (n : Nat) -> (own_heap_auth sigma).upred_holds n a0 =>
      \lam n => inP (M.unit,
                     transport (\lam w => M.dist n a0 w)
                         (inv (ucmra_unit_right_id a0))
                         (M.ofe_dist_refl n a0))
    | h_ghost : properUPred_ent
        (own_heap_auth sigma)
        (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi)) =>
      ghost_intro e Phi sigma hwp
    | h_seed : properUPred_ent
        (own_heap_auth sigma)
        (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi))) =>
      properUPred_ent_trans
          (own_heap_auth sigma)
          (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi))
          (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi)))
          h_ghost
          (bupd_intro (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi)))
    | h_run : properUPred_ent
        (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi)))
        (bupd_later_iter k
            (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp (Val v) Phi)))) =>
      wp_steps k e (Val v) Phi sigma sigma' hsteps
    | wp_val_eq : upredEquiv (wp (Val v) Phi) (mkProperBUpd (Phi v)) =>
      wp_value v Phi
    | wp_val_to_bupd : properUPred_ent (wp (Val v) Phi) (mkProperBUpd (Phi v)) =>
      \lam n a hv h => (wp_val_eq n a hv).1 h
    | sep_inner_mono : properUPred_ent
        (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp (Val v) Phi))
        (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (mkProperBUpd (Phi v))) =>
      \lam n a hv hsep =>
          \case hsep \with {
            | inP (a1, a2, dist_a, h1, h2) =>
              \let
                | M2 => HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value
                | hv_op : M2.validN n (M2.op a1 a2) =>
                  M2.cmra_validN_ne n a (M2.op a1 a2) dist_a hv
                | hv_a2 : M2.validN n a2 =>
                  M2.cmra_validN_op_l n a2 a1
                      (transport (\lam w => M2.validN n w) (M2.cmra_comm a1 a2) hv_op)
              \in inP (a1, a2, dist_a, h1, wp_val_to_bupd n a2 hv_a2 h2)
          }
    | step_collapsed : properUPred_ent
        (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp (Val v) Phi)))
        (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (mkProperBUpd (Phi v)))) =>
      bupd_mono
          (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp (Val v) Phi))
          (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (mkProperBUpd (Phi v)))
          sep_inner_mono
    | h_run_unfolded : properUPred_ent
        (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi)))
        (bupd_later_iter k
            (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma')
                (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v)))))) =>
      properUPred_ent_trans
          (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi)))
          (bupd_later_iter k
              (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp (Val v) Phi))))
          (bupd_later_iter k
              (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma')
                  (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v))))))
          h_run
          (iter_mono_aux k
              (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp (Val v) Phi)))
              (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (mkProperBUpd (Phi v))))
              step_collapsed)
    | inner_drop : properUPred_ent
        (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma')
            (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v))))
        (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v))) =>
      \lam n' a' hv' hsep =>
          \case hsep \with {
            | inP (a1, a2, dist_a, _, h_bupd_pure) =>
                  (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v))).upred_mono n' n' a2 a'
                  h_bupd_pure
                  (inP (a1,
                        M.ofe_dist_trans n' a' (M.op a1 a2) (M.op a2 a1)
                            dist_a
                            (transport (\lam w => M.dist n' (M.op a1 a2) w)
                                (M.cmra_comm a1 a2)
                                (M.ofe_dist_refl n' (M.op a1 a2)))))
                  <=-refl
          }
    | h_collapsed_step : properUPred_ent
        (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma')
            (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v)))))
        (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v))) =>
      properUPred_ent_trans
          (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma')
              (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v)))))
          (mkProperBUpd (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v))))
          (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v)))
          (bupd_mono
              (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v))))
              (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v)))
              inner_drop)
          (bupd_trans (mkProperPure (phi v)))
    | h_iter_pure : properUPred_ent
        (bupd_later_iter k
            (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma')
                (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v))))))
        (bupd_later_iter k (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v)))) =>
      iter_mono_aux k _ _ h_collapsed_step
    | h_final : properUPred_ent
        (own_heap_auth sigma)
        (bupd_later_iter k (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v)))) =>
      properUPred_ent_trans
          (own_heap_auth sigma)
          (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi)))
          (bupd_later_iter k (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v))))
          h_seed
          (properUPred_ent_trans
              (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi)))
              (bupd_later_iter k
                  (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma')
                      (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v))))))
              (bupd_later_iter k (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v))))
              h_run_unfolded
              h_iter_pure)
    | h_at_k : (bupd_later_iter k (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (phi v)))).upred_holds k a0 =>
      h_final k a0 (hv_a0 k) (hauth_a0 k)
  \in bupd_later_iter_soundness k (phi v) a0 (hv_a0 k) h_at_k
  \where {
    -- | Monotonicity of the `(|==> ▷)ʲ` tower in its argument predicate: from `P ⊢ Q`
    -- | derive `bupd_later_iter j P ⊢ bupd_later_iter j Q`. Proved by induction on `j`,
    -- | applying `bupd_mono` under each `▷` layer (peeling one step index via `cmra_validN_le`).
    \lemma iter_mono_aux
      {cnt : Countable Loc}
      (j : Nat)
      (P Q : ProperUPred (HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value))
      (hPQ : properUPred_ent P Q)
      : properUPred_ent (bupd_later_iter j P) (bupd_later_iter j Q)
    \elim j
      | 0 => hPQ
      | suc j' =>
        bupd_mono
            (mkProperLater (bupd_later_iter j' P))
            (mkProperLater (bupd_later_iter j' Q))
            (\lam n a hv hl =>
                \case n \as n', hv \as hv' : (HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value).validN n' a,
                      hl \as hl' :
                          (mkProperLater (bupd_later_iter j' P)).upred_holds n' a
                \return (mkProperLater (bupd_later_iter  j' Q)).upred_holds n' a
                \with {
                  | 0, _, _ => ()
                  | suc m, hv_sm, hl_inner =>
                    iter_mono_aux j' P Q hPQ m a
                        ((HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value).cmra_validN_le (suc m) m a hv_sm (n<=sucn m))
                        hl_inner
                })
  }


-- | Progress / safety half of adequacy: if `True ⊢ wp e {v. ⌜φ v⌝}` and `(e, σ)` reduces
-- | in `k` steps to `(e', σ')`, then `(e', σ')` is `not_stuck` — i.e. `e'` is a value or
-- | can step further. Together with `wp_adequacy` this gives the full type-safety statement:
-- | well-specified programs never get stuck.
-- |
-- | Proof mirrors `wp_adequacy` but ends in `wp_not_stuck` instead of `wp_value`:
-- | seed (`ghost_intro` + `bupd_intro`), run the `k` steps (`wp_steps`) to obtain
-- | `S(σ') ∗ wp e' {Φ}` under the modal tower, convert that to `|==> ⌜not_stuck e' σ'⌝`
-- | (`wp_not_stuck`, flattening with `bupd_trans`), push it through the tower with
-- | `iter_mono_aux`, and extract the pure result at index `k` via `bupd_later_iter_soundness`.
\lemma wp_progress
  {cnt : Countable Loc}
  (e      : Expr)
  (phi    : Value -> \Prop)
  (sigma  : State cnt)
  (k      : Nat)
  (e'     : Expr)
  (sigma' : State cnt)
  (hwp    : properUPred_ent
      (mkProperPure (\Sigma))
      (wp e (\lam w => mkProperPure (phi w))))
  (hsteps : Steps k e sigma e' sigma')
  : not_stuck e' sigma' =>
  \let
    | M => HeapCMRA Loc cnt Value
    | Phi : Value -> ProperUPred M => \lam w => mkProperPure (phi w)
    | a0 => heap_auth (heap_state_to_gmap sigma)
    | hv_a0 : \Pi (n : Nat) -> M.validN n a0 =>
      \lam n =>
          \let
            | G => GmapUCMRA Loc cnt (ExclUCMRA (DiscreteOFE Value))
            | g => heap_state_to_gmap sigma
            | hv_g : G.validN n g => heap_state_to_gmap_validN n sigma
            | hincl : inclN {G} {\new Op G.E { | op => G.op }} gempty n g =>
              inP (g, transport (\lam w => G.dist n g w)
                  (inv (G.ucmra_unit_left_id g))
                  (G.ofe_dist_refl n g))
          \in (hv_g, hincl)
    | hauth_a0 : \Pi (n : Nat) -> (own_heap_auth sigma).upred_holds n a0 =>
      \lam n => inP (M.unit,
                     transport (\lam w => M.dist n a0 w)
                         (inv (ucmra_unit_right_id a0))
                         (M.ofe_dist_refl n a0))

    | h_seed : properUPred_ent
        (own_heap_auth sigma)
        (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi))) =>
      properUPred_ent_trans
          (own_heap_auth sigma)
          (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi))
          (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi)))
          (ghost_intro e Phi sigma hwp)
          (bupd_intro (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi)))
    | h_run : properUPred_ent
        (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi)))
        (bupd_later_iter k
            (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp e' Phi)))) =>
      wp_steps k e e' Phi sigma sigma' hsteps
    | step_to_pure : properUPred_ent
        (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp e' Phi))
        (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (not_stuck e' sigma'))) =>
      wp_not_stuck e' Phi sigma'
    | collapse : properUPred_ent
        (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp e' Phi)))
        (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (not_stuck e' sigma'))) =>
      properUPred_ent_trans
          (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp e' Phi)))
          (mkProperBUpd (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (not_stuck e' sigma'))))
          (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (not_stuck e' sigma')))
          (bupd_mono
              (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp e' Phi))
              (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (not_stuck e' sigma')))
              step_to_pure)
          (bupd_trans (mkProperPure (not_stuck e' sigma')))
    | h_iter : properUPred_ent
        (bupd_later_iter k
            (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp e' Phi))))
        (bupd_later_iter k
            (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (not_stuck e' sigma')))) =>
      wp_adequacy.iter_mono_aux k _ _ collapse

    | h_final : properUPred_ent
        (own_heap_auth sigma)
        (bupd_later_iter k (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (not_stuck e' sigma')))) =>
      properUPred_ent_trans
          (own_heap_auth sigma)
          (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi)))
          (bupd_later_iter k (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (not_stuck e' sigma'))))
          h_seed
          (properUPred_ent_trans
              (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma) (wp e Phi)))
              (bupd_later_iter k
                  (mkProperBUpd (mkProperSep (own_heap_auth sigma') (wp e' Phi))))
              (bupd_later_iter k (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (not_stuck e' sigma'))))
              h_run h_iter)

    | h_at_k : (bupd_later_iter k
        (mkProperBUpd (mkProperPure (not_stuck e' sigma')))).upred_holds k a0 =>
      h_final k a0 (hv_a0 k) (hauth_a0 k)
  \in bupd_later_iter_soundness k (not_stuck e' sigma') a0 (hv_a0 k) h_at_k
```
